NAME
       ifconfig - show or configure network interfaces

SYNOPSIS
       ifconfig
       ifconfig <iface> <address> [netmask] [gateway] [dns]

DESCRIPTION
       With no arguments, lists every interface with its link state,
       MTU, hardware address, addresses and packet counters, including
       drops.

       With arguments, assigns a static configuration to IFACE. This
       replaces whatever DHCP set up.

EXAMPLES
       ifconfig
       ifconfig eth0 192.168.1.50 255.255.255.0 192.168.1.1 8.8.8.8

SEE ALSO
       ip(1), ping(1), setdns(1), nslookup(1)
